1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,080
Good morning, and welcome to City Football Club.

2
00:00:04,080 --> 00:00:09,661
I'd like to give you some useful information about your visit to the stadium today,

3
00:00:09,661 --> 00:00:15,940
and then we'll start the tour of the areas of the stadium that are open to visitors.

4
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:19,060
I can see lots of children here today

5
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:23,690
so just to let mums and dads know a few things before we start.

6
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:28,900
The stadium has lots of stairs, and the players' tunnel is very dark.

7
00:00:28,900 --> 00:00:34,780
Please don't let your children wander off on their own, even for a minute.

8
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:38,700
We don't want any accidents or anyone getting frightened.

9
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:45,990
Cameras are permitted everywhere, and you can take pictures of your child shooting a penalty.

10
00:00:45,990 --> 00:00:48,323
Assistants are helping to organise this,

11
00:00:48,323 --> 00:00:52,360
and hopefully the queue won't be too long

12
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:56,100
it's very hot and sunny out on the pitch today.

13
00:00:56,100 --> 00:01:04,580
You can get food and drink at the café, and I really recommend the healthy lunch boxes for children.

14
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:11,410
Also in the café, children are invited to do a football-themed drawing.

15
00:01:11,410 --> 00:01:15,896
We'll pick the best one at the end of the afternoon,

16
00:01:15,896 --> 00:01:21,130
so don't forget to put your name and contact details on the back.

17
00:01:21,130 --> 00:01:26,260
That way, if you've left the stadium before then, we'll send your prize

18
00:01:26,540 --> 00:01:29,810
but sadly we can't return drawings.

19
00:01:29,810 --> 00:01:34,280
I'd like to mention some features of the tour.

20
00:01:34,280 --> 00:01:38,200
We'll start with the three-sixty cinema experience

21
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:41,445
which has been very popular over the years,

22
00:01:41,445 --> 00:01:44,300
and then I'll take you to the players

23
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:50,850
dressing rooms before going outside to the seating area and the pitch.

24
00:01:50,850 --> 00:01:59,194
I should say, if you'd prefer your visit to be self-guided, please collect headphones from the reception

25
00:01:59,194 --> 00:02:05,220
and then you can listen to the pre-recorded information at your own speed.

26
00:02:05,220 --> 00:02:11,180
We've only just introduced this feature, and would appreciate your feedback.

27
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:15,540
We're thinking of offering tours in other languages in future

28
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:18,970
so if you have any thoughts on that,

29
00:02:18,970 --> 00:02:21,020
we'd welcome those too.

30
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:28,313
If you plan to return another time, you might like to book one of our VIP tours -

31
00:02:28,313 --> 00:02:33,890
we've only just started offering these, and they can be booked online.

32
00:02:33,890 --> 00:02:38,640
Now, the stadium you see today was built in 1989

33
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:41,849
as part of a three-year redevelopment project

34
00:02:41,849 --> 00:02:45,140
while that project was going on

35
00:02:45,480 --> 00:02:50,744
the team had to play its matches at the ground of another club -

36
00:02:50,744 --> 00:02:56,830
apart from that, the club has been here on this site since 1870.

37
00:02:56,830 --> 00:02:59,246
As some of you may know,

38
00:02:59,246 --> 00:03:06,090
that was the start of a really important decade in the history of football in this country.

39
00:03:06,090 --> 00:03:13,600
For example, 1870 was also the year that football teams started to include a player

40
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:16,470
whose role it was to guard the goal.

41
00:03:16,470 --> 00:03:24,790
It's hard to imagine what the game must have been like without someone in that position, isn't it?

42
00:03:24,790 --> 00:03:30,340
In 1872 and 73, many other clubs were established

43
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:34,540
both here and abroad, and the following year,

44
00:03:34,540 --> 00:03:39,440
in 1874, referees were allowed to send players off

45
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:42,570
if they committed certain offences.

46
00:03:42,570 --> 00:03:49,340
And also in that year, teams started having to swap ends at half-time.

47
00:03:49,340 --> 00:03:54,774
One fact I was interested to discover was that in early football games,

48
00:03:54,774 --> 00:04:00,626
the aim was for the scorer to get the ball between two flag posts,

49
00:04:00,626 --> 00:04:06,060
and later between sticks joined at the top with a piece of tape.

50
00:04:06,060 --> 00:04:15,070
In 1875, that tape was replaced with the solid crossbar that we're familiar with today.

51
00:04:15,070 --> 00:04:19,820
1877 saw the founding of further new clubs

52
00:04:19,820 --> 00:04:23,597
and the history books tell us that in the same year,

53
00:04:23,597 --> 00:04:29,880
all the clubs decided to set a limit of ninety minutes for each match.

54
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:33,460
Before that, it was a more casual arrangement

55
00:04:33,980 --> 00:04:36,219
and this sometimes caused huge arguments -

56
00:04:36,219 --> 00:04:42,558
and sometimes fights - during matches, when one team called the end of the game

57
00:04:42,558 --> 00:04:49,350
and the other team wanted to play on to try and score a winning goal.

58
00:04:49,350 --> 00:04:56,290
By 1878, the number of teams in the football league increased again.

59
00:04:56,290 --> 00:04:59,660
In addition, referees started using whistles

60
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:04,610
and electric lamps were installed on certain pitches.

61
00:05:04,610 --> 00:05:08,360
This was a significant change, as games could

62
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:12,990
then be played in the evenings all year round.

63
00:05:12,990 --> 00:05:18,655
In 1880, clubs began to charge fans for admission to games,

64
00:05:18,655 --> 00:05:24,320
even though players were still amateurs and had other 'proper' jobs.

65
00:05:24,320 --> 00:05:28,140
That's hard to imagine in the modern professional game

66
00:05:28,140 --> 00:05:35,230
where top players earn significant sums of money from both playing and commercial activities.
